e  remaining survivors reached something  strange in the water it's a high-rise  building meaning the whole of japan has  officially sunk alright this is not  looking good we've been sitting here for  what seems like ages and we can't tell  how much time has passed because the sky  is blocked by ash and smoke this also  means that it's nearly impossible for  anyone flying overhead to see us this  group got extremely lucky and likely  wouldn't have made it in any other  scenario we can't use the sun's  reflection through a piece of mirror or  our phone screens to alert any nearby  planes or ships nor from the looks of  things can we use any non-porous  materials like a raincoat to catch and  store drinkable rainwater based on what  muto told us volcanic ash has polluted  the air meaning any rain water we  collect will be unsafe to drink however  desperate times call for desperate  measures so i would carefully consume  small amounts of collected ash water but  only as a last resort since we would be  stranded here for a long time small  amounts of ash taken through the water  in limited quantities could present a  low risk of toxicity in this situation  we have little choice the longer we  remain stranded muto and goher missed  out on a big opportunity to take a break  on top of the sunken building they could  have used that place as a base whilst  they waited out the rescue as this would  have also ensured that they don't get  pushed further out into sea or be at the  mercy of any rogue waves and while this  might sound counterproductive instead of  eating the chocolate bar they should  have fought off their hunger and used it  as bait to catch fish yes you heard me  right according to our friend famous  survivalist michael halworth in his book  the sea survival manual fish are  attracted to vessels and boats this  means if muto had any jewelry on her or  if she used pieces of her phone she  could have used this as a makeshift lure  to attract fish to her area and she  could have used her shoelaces or unravel  sock threads to serve as a fishing line  after a few days at sea the group starts  to get sick and weak suddenly during  that night muto here wakes up and  notices the old guy hunched over the  tent wall with some nice seagulls  viciously attacking him chewing them  away she looks over and notices  something extremely horrifying the man  has been dead for hours and the seagulls  have peeled his skin from flesh suddenly  a shark comes out of nowhere and takes  them away muto here zips the tent up and  the two wait until help arrives after a  few days out on sea mom and glasses guy  here finally find the kids before they  starve to death glasses guy shows them  coordinates left by mr onodera and goher  figures out that they must be located  east of hiroshima using a self-made  compass they figure out exactly where  the closest shore is and head off a  stranded motorboat is then spotted out  of the blue but unlucky for them it's  stuck volunteering to fix the issue mom  here dives in and tries to dislodge the  rope she manages to dislodge it  successfully but before she makes it to  the surface she drowns before anything  can be done okay mom took one for the  team here and this is exactly why it's  good to have people with different skill  sets take turns risking their lives this  way they can get the group out of sticky  situations while we sit back and relax  and since the motor is placed in the  back i'm willing to take a guess that  the boat had a v-drive inboard system  rather than a direct drive system which  would have had the motor placed in the  middle of the boat this means that this  is no easy feat but someone could have  tried reversing the bow just slightly  enough to loosen the tension on the rope  which would have made it easier to help  mom pull out the rope giving her a few  precious extra seconds to swim back to  the surface if this sounds too  complicated then it probably is mom here  is a pro swimmer but her glory days  might be behind her she should have been  able to hold her breath for much longer  and known that swimming rapidly upwards  from deep water to the surface would  cause her to pass out she could have  easily survived the situation by taking  a moment to physically and mentally  prepare her body to withstand the  underwater pressure by inhaling and  exhaling slowly from deep within her  diaphragm we can rid the lungs of low  quality air preparing for it to intake  excess oxygen to be stored within the  blood cells applying this technique for  a few minutes would have ultimately  helped her increase the amount of time  she could have held her breath while it  might seem difficult she only needed a  few more seconds and she would have made  it back to the boat safe and sound some  time later a japanese tank approaches  them suddenly kite appears and invites  them in with mr onodera also chilling  with him as well after a turbulent trip  they finally make it to land and find a  nearby hot spring after a well-deserved  break kite here takes the group to the  only place in japan that can withstand a  natural disaster he knows of a place  with secret archives that might hold the  information to be able to save the  entire country from any further damage  exploring the island they find a secret  cape but kite here decides to go it  alone with onodera walking inside they  find a secret research room with the  files he was looking for as kite manages  to transfer the files into a hard drive  a roaring earthquake then trembles once  again hitting the island as the room  begins to fill with water using an  oxygen tank he and onodera managed to  swim back to the surface but they're not  safe just yet strong waves begin to hit  the island and the hard drive gets swept  away in the process it's dangerous but  glasses guy here decides to go fetch the  files after an absolutely epic sprint he  grabs the data chip and nearly makes it  back to safety he tosses the data chip  to the gang right before a massive wave  slams right into him from the side  killing him if we think about it for a  second he was our best bet since he had  extensive experience in track and field  muto here is also an athlete but her leg  is injured and her only other options  were a kid a youtuber and a paraplegic  meaning we don't have many options  judging from the rough stone coastline  that area looked pretty deadly even if  this guy was a professional big wave  surfer you would have still been dragged  into the stone coastline or the seabed  itself and there's little chance of  surviving that if i were glasses guy  instead of waiting for wave to come and  go and then run i would have begun  running as soon as the waves came  crashing into me this would have been a  little riskier but would have given us a  whole extra second meaning we have 11  seconds not 10 to make it back and an  extra second was all that this guy  needed if he timed it better checking  the archives they find a ray of hope  onodera predicted exactly which areas  would sink as well as which areas would  rise back up meaning parts of japan will  return in coming years using a raft they  find a hot air balloon floating in the  ocean kite manages to fill it using a  spare oxygen tank but the balloon only  has room for one so kite here decides to  fly away on his own leaving the rest for  dead jerk checking mr onodera's body  they find a working phone with a working  internet connection it turns out the  kite used the hot air balloon to find an  internet signal alerting their location  to rescue services and that's when a  helicopter comes and picks them up all  due to kite now they're safe while  looking over the ravaged japanese  landscape muto suddenly passes out due  to the cut on her leg she's taken to the  hospital and operated on a doctor  informs her that due to the infection on  her leg she's developed superrative  osteomyelitis a condition which will  kill her and the only way to stop the  infection from killing her is to  amputate her leg eight years later japan  has risen once again muto here is  competing at the 2028 paralympics with a  prosthetic leg remembering all that  she's lost she completes her dream of  being a world-class athlete marking her  legacy in the history books and if you  want to join the history books along  with muto then i suggest you comment  down below let us know what you liked  what you didn't like don't forget to  give us a big thumbs up and don't forget  to subscribe to our channel and also  don't forget to check out our playlist  and our tech talk page
 

